# Build outputs. The PDFs are the deliverable but they are 90 MB across the
# four papers; rebuild them with `pdflatex <name>` twice, or take them from a
# release. The bodies themselves are generated too -- see README.md -- but they
# ARE tracked, so that a reader of the repository can read the papers without
# running the generator.
#
# anon/*.pdf falls under the *.pdf rule below and is NOT tracked. Rebuild with:
#
#     python3 make-anon-figures.py
#
# Do not skip it. Paper D's \graphicspath lists anon/ first and ../ after, so a
# missing anonymised figure does not fail the build -- pdflatex silently falls
# back to the BRANDED plot, exits 0, and produces a ten-page PDF that names the
# project on page 6 and would be rejected without review. Verified by deleting
# it: the build stayed green and only `python3 make-series.py` went red. That
# PDF gate is the thing standing between a clean log and a rejected submission.
*.aux
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.pdf
!../*.pdf
